design\feature_descriptions\F_122_show_conversation_context_window_usage.md:18:The Codex App Server emits `thread/tokenUsage/updated` with the latest request usage in `tokenUsage.last` and the effective capacity in `tokenUsage.modelContextWindow`. `agent_streaming_adapter.js` keeps the latest token counters but discards the context-window capacity. The runner then accumulates those counters into `AgentConversation.usage`, which is suitable for total usage but cannot represent current context occupancy.
design\feature_descriptions\F_122_show_conversation_context_window_usage.md:24:- Preserve a separate latest context-window snapshot on Codex conversations: `usedTokens` from `tokenUsage.last.totalTokens` and `capacityTokens` from `tokenUsage.modelContextWindow`. Do not add these values to cumulative `AgentTokenUsage` or its shared aggregation helpers.
